From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 14:54:12 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_sandbox, settings_ui: Hide the Kernel -- uname and
 sysinfo from ai-jail
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

docs/HOST-VIEW-EXTRA-LAYER.md §4.3/§4.4, the Zeo side of step 2 (operator,
2026-11-23: step 2 first among the remaining asks).

ai-jail 3.5.0-r4 (the fork's feat/syscall-view) adds --syscall-view under
--mask-host: a seccomp user-notify filter sends uname(2) and sysinfo(2) to
ai-jail outside the jail, which answers with the cleaned kernel strings and
the jail's limits. Without it `uname -r`, Python's platform and
`getconf _PHYS_PAGES` kept the host's values while the host view's files
said otherwise.

What changes here, on the same lines as 0160's overlay switch:
- probe.rs reads --syscall-view from ai-jail --help (supports_syscall_view).
- HostLayer gains syscall_view; host_args_for passes --syscall-view after
  --mask-host (and --overlay-system) when the project asks for it.
- agent_sandbox.syscall_view (default false, per project). It applies only
  with mask_host; a project that asks for it from an ai-jail without the
  option is refused (LaunchCause::SyscallViewUnsupported,
  cause=syscall_view_unsupported). The settings fingerprint includes it.
- The Agent Sandbox page's Host section: "Hide the Kernel"
  (set_project_syscall_view), disabled with Hide the Disks' note while the
  host is shown.

Why off by default: every process in the jail pays a round trip to ai-jail
on those two calls; §4.4 keeps it off until it has run in daily use.

Tests: host_view_tests (the overlay test now also expects --syscall-view
last, and neither flag without the host view); host_view_layer_tests
(passes --syscall-view after --mask-host, refused without the option);
agent_jail_host_tests (the switch follows the project and is disabled
with the host shown).
---

